  "commit_summaries": [
    "31edb275d3bbc57e655c02e3a019f6646cabf0c1\n2026-11-05T15:23:12+09:00\nRebuild the workbench as an agent desk with MuJoCo physics preview\n\nThe workbench becomes a task conversation with a layered side pane behind\nthe same 4100 entry. The seven dock workspaces are recomposed into\nalgorithms, simulation, maps, experiments, library and settings; every\npanel keeps a home and the free layout stays available.\n\nAlgorithm library: classes ranked for a chosen map, then per-algorithm\nconditions, parameters, versions, references, local run record, head-to-head\nresults on identical inputs, and side-by-side trials on any map.\n\nPhysics: mujoco_field runs the frozen field plan with the same follower,\nmission queue, vehicle parameters and control rates as the Gazebo session,\nin its own process, without ROS. sim2sim replays a finished Gazebo session\nand reports the gap between the two engines. Only the ideal configuration is\nmodelled; anything else is refused rather than approximated.\n\nHarness (agent-runner/5, agent-prompts/4): every verified plan meets the\nphysics engine before the report, the best plan that passed goes to Gazebo,\nand the runner stays with an approved simulation until it ends so the report\nstates what happened. Sessions gain short titles, pin, archive and rename.\nCapabilities and background jobs from every backend are listed in one place.\n\nfieldcheck.track_check is extracted so both engines face the same test.\nMuJoCo 3.17.0 joins the lab lock file.\n\nEvidence is in setup/2026-11-05/desk and experiments/agent-evals/20261105-*,\nwith the summary at the top of the integration report.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "82db23521565a27ffd585a70ed49f07a4eff165e\n2026-11-05T21:47:39+09:00\nPackage the workbench as a desktop app with key-only model providers\n\nModels: pick a service from the models.dev catalog, paste an API key and\nuse it. Keys stay in the private credentials file and are verified on the\nprovider's model list. The local Ollama path is removed.\n\nDesktop: src/desktop wraps the same interface in Electron and starts a\nbundled Python backend, with AppImage, deb and NSIS targets. History data\ndownloads inside the app as a checked pack. Gazebo comes from the simulation\nimage through the container backend on both platforms. Updates and the\nLinux and Windows builds follow a v* tag in .github/workflows/desktop.yml.\n\nMachines without ROS: the official maps ship as unmodified copies, and the\nsimulation page says up front where Gazebo comes from.\n\nWindows: process control lives in urp_lab/compat.py, the runtime database\nflushes through a writable handle, and the Microsoft runtime DLLs are packed.\n\nAccepted on the packages from this tree: AppImage, deb on clean Ubuntu,\nno-ROS Linux, the Windows installer and shell under Wine, and the container\npath with real Docker and Gazebo. Real Windows has not been run yet; the\nreport lists the scope and evidence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
  ]
